From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2026 10:12:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/rockchip: use a translated domain for IOMMU masters

The masters behind rockchip-iommu are media blocks: the display
controller, the video codecs, the ISP and the 2D engine. They are wired
to the IOMMU so that their buffers do not have to be physically
contiguous. With a system-wide passthrough default, which is what
IOMMU_DEFAULT_PASSTHROUGH gives, those masters are handed an identity
domain instead, and every buffer has to come from CMA. A 4K frame needs
15.8 MiB of it, so hardware decoding fails the allocation and falls back
to software.

Return IOMMU_DOMAIN_DMA from def_domain_type so these masters get a
translated domain whatever the system default is, the way apple-dart
does for its no-bypass configurations. Masters behind other IOMMUs are
untouched, so a PCIe root port behind an SMMU keeps the system default
and its performance.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
--- a/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
@@ -1166,12 +1166,19 @@ static int rk_iommu_of_xlate(struct devi
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* An identity domain would put these media masters back onto CMA. */
+static int rk_iommu_def_domain_type(struct device *dev)
+{
+	return IOMMU_DOMAIN_DMA;
+}
+
 static const struct iommu_ops rk_iommu_ops = {
 	.identity_domain = &rk_identity_domain,
 	.domain_alloc_paging = rk_iommu_domain_alloc_paging,
 	.probe_device = rk_iommu_probe_device,
 	.release_device = rk_iommu_release_device,
 	.device_group = generic_single_device_group,
+	.def_domain_type = rk_iommu_def_domain_type,
 	.of_xlate = rk_iommu_of_xlate,
 	.default_domain_ops = &(const struct iommu_domain_ops) {
 		.attach_dev	= rk_iommu_attach_device,
